    "processes": [],
    "headline": "Manugareru is from Old Japanese 免る (manukaru), 目 (ma-, “eye”) plus 抜かる (nukaru, “to mistake”).",
    "morphemes": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "quote": "From Old Japanese 免る (manukaru), in the 下(しも)二(に)段(だん)活(かつ)用(よう) (shimo nidan katsuyō, “lower bigrade conjugation”) pattern, from 目(ま) (ma-, “eye”) + 抜(ぬ)かる (nukaru, “to mistake”)."
      },
      {
        "quote": "Development"
      },
      {
        "quote": "Natural progression from Old and Classical Japanese 下(しも)二(に)段(だん)活(かつ)用(よう) (shimo nidan katsuyō, “lower bigrade conjugation”) verbs ending in -u to modern Japanese 下(しも)一(いち)段(だん)活(かつ)用(よう) (shimo ichidan katsuyō, “lower monograde conjugation”) verbs ending in -eru."
      }
    ],
    "wiktionaryDump": "2026-09-02"
  },
